Fu-k&#39;ang-an\">Fu-k'ang-an</a></div><div class=\"wst-header-forward-arrow\">\u2192</div></div></div><div class=\"wst-header-notes header&#95;notes searchaux wst-unknown-notes\"><style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r14791120\">.mw-parser-output .plainSister{display:block;font-size:93%;line-height:normal;list-style-type:none;list-style-image:none;list-style-position:outside;border:1px solid var(--border-color-interactive--hover,#AAA);float:right;clear:right;margin:0.5ex 0 0.5ex 0.5ex;padding:0;background:var(--background-color-base,#FFFFFF);color:var(--color-base,#202122)}.mw-parser-output .sisicon,.mw-parser-output .dabicon{padding-right:1ex}</style><ul class=\"plainSister\"><li class=\"sisitem\"><span class=\"sisicon\"><span typeof=\"mw:File/Frameless\"><a href=\"/wiki/Special:SiteMatrix\" title=\"Special:SiteMatrix\"><img alt=\"Sister Projects\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Wikimedia-logo.svg/20px-Wikimedia-logo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikisource.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Wikimedia-logo.svg/40px-Wikimedia-logo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikisource.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"1024\" data-file-height=\"1024\" /></a></span></span><a href=\"/wiki/Special:SiteMatrix\" title=\"Special:SiteMatrix\">sister projects</a>: <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q107367192\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"d:Q107367192\">Wikidata item</a></li></ul></div><div class=\"ws-noexport\" id=\"ws-data\" style=\"speak:none\"><span id=\"ws-article-id\">3639191</span><span id=\"ws-title\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period\">Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period</a>, Volume 1 \u2014 Fu I-chien</span><span id=\"ws-editor\">Arthur W. Hummel</span><span id=\"ws-author\">Fang Chao-ying</span></div></div>\n<p><span style=\"display:none\" id=\"dynamic&#95;layout&#95;overrider\">Layout 2</span>\n</p>\n<div class=\"prp-pages-output\" lang=\"en\">\n<p><span><span class=\"pagenum ws-pagenum\" id=\"253\" data-page-number=\"253\" data-page-name=\"Page:Eminent Chinese Of The Ch\u2019ing Period - Hummel - 1943 - Vol. 1.pdf/265\" data-page-index=\"265\" data-page-quality=\"4\" title=\"Page:Eminent&#95;Chinese&#95;Of&#95;The&#95;Ch%E2%80%99ing&#95;Period&#95;-&#95;Hummel&#95;-&#95;1943&#95;-&#95;Vol.&#95;1.pdf/265\"><span id=\"pageindex&#95;265\" class=\"pagenum-inner ws-noexport\">&#8203;</span></span></span><b>FU</b> I-chien \u5085\u4ee5\u6f38 (<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r14767791\">.mw-parser-output .wst-tooltip{cursor:help;border-bottom:thin dotted cornflowerblue}.mw-parser-output .wst-tooltip-nodash{border-bottom:none}</style><span class=\"wst-tooltip wst-tooltip-dash\" title=\"Courtesy name (Tz\u00fb/Zi, \u5b57)\">T.</span>&#160;\u4e8e\u78ec,&#32;<link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r14767791\" /><span class=\"wst-tooltip wst-tooltip-dash\" title=\"Literary name (Hao, \u865f)\">H.</span>&#160;\u661f\u5dd6), 1609\u20131665, was a native of Liao'ch'\u00eang, Shantung. He took his <i>chin-shih</i> with highest honors in 1646, and so was the first scholar to receive the degree of <i>chuang-y\u00fcan</i> \u72c0\u5143 or <i>optimus</i> in the Ch'ing dynasty. Made a first class compiler in the Hung w\u00ean-y\u00fcan \u5f18\u6587\u9662, he was promoted through successive offices to the post of a Grand Secretary in 1654. In 1657 he and Ts'ao P\u00ean-jung \u66f9\u672c\u69ae (ca. 1621\u2014ca. 1664) were ordered to compile a comprehensive commentary to the <i>Classic of Changes</i>\u2014a task which they completed in the next year under the title \u6613\u7d93\u901a\u6ce8 <i>I-ching t'ung-chu</i>, in 9 <i>ch\u00fcan</i>. Shortly thereafter he asked leave, on grounds of illness, to return to his home. He was allowed to retire in 1661.\n</p><p>Fu I-chien was stout and bearded. He had an adopted son, whose great-grandson, Fu Sh\u00eang-hs\u00fcn \u5085\u7e69\u52db (<link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r14767791\" /><span class=\"wst-tooltip wst-tooltip-dash\" title=\"Courtesy name (Tz\u00fb/Zi, \u5b57)\">T.</span>&#160;\u63a5\u6b66, \u548c\u8ed2,&#32;<link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r14767791\" /><span class=\"wst-tooltip wst-tooltip-dash\" title=\"Literary name (Hao, \u865f)\">H.</span>&#160;\u79cb\u576a, \u53e4\u6751,&#32;<i>chin-shih</i> of 1814), served as governor of Kiangsi (1848\u201349), and of Kiangsu (1849\u201351).\n</p>\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r15431518\">.mw-parser-output .wst-rule{background-color:currentcolor;color:inherit;width:auto;margin:2px auto 2px auto;height:1px;overflow:hidden}.mw-parser-output .wst-rule.wst-rule-left{margin-left:0}.mw-parser-output .wst-rule.wst-rule-right{margin-right:0}.mw-parser-output .wst-rule.__uirule{background-color:#a2a9b1;color:inherit;border:0;margin-top:0.2em;margin-bottom:0.2em}</style><hr class=\"wst-rule wst-rule-center\" style=\"color:inherit;\" />\n<p>[1/224/4b; 2/5/39a; <i>I-ching t'ung-chu</i> (4 <i>ch\u00fcan</i> edition) in \u6e56\u5317\u53e2\u66f8 <i>Hupeh ts'ung-shu</i>; <i>Liao-ch'\u00eang hsien-chih</i> (1910) 8/44b; <i>ibid</i>, \u8006\u737b\u6587\u5fb5, \u4e2d19a, \u4e0b10a.]\n</p>\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r15431519\">.mw-parser-output .wst-right{text-align:right}</style><div class=\"wst-right\" style=\"margin-right:2em;\">\n<p><span class=\"smallcaps\" style=\"font-variant:small-caps;\">Fang Chao-ying</span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<p><br />\n&#32;\n</p>\n</div>\n</div>"},"links":[{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Fu-k'ang-an"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Fu I"},{"ns":102,"exists":"","*":"Author:Arthur W. Hummel"},{"ns":102,"exists":"","*":"Author:Fang Chao-ying"}],"sections":[],"wikitext":{"*":"{{Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period\n | volume   = 1\n | onlysection = fu i-chien\n | previous = Fu I\n | next     = Fu-k'ang-an\n | from     = 265\n | to       = 265\n | notes    = \n | section_author = Fang Chao-ying\n}}{{DEFAULTSORT:Fu I-chien}}"}}}